[[Enzo Mari]], Italy, 1973 or 1974, depending on the source. From [[Autoprogettazione]].

Pine boards, nails, and a hammer. Mari gave out the plans so people could build the furniture themselves.

One of the places today's [[DIY]] and maker culture comes from. This is in the [[F/LOSD]] space as well — here's an idea, please make it yourself, share and improve. A different kind of [[Vernacular]] design perhaps too?

[[Mari building one himself, for Artek|https://vimeo.com/39624485]].

